# ArduPilot GeoFence: the last-line backstop behind the Safety Shield.
#
# Grant, Architecture constraints p1: "The autopilot's own GeoFence /
# FENCE_ACTION is the ultimate backstop." Loaded by sitl/start_sitl.sh as an
# extra --defaults file after the stock copter.parm (GUARDRAIL_FENCE=0 skips
# it). Parameter meanings are from ArduCopter 4.5.7,
# libraries/AC_Fence/AC_Fence.cpp.
#
# The polygons come from the POLICY, not from this file: the MAVLink adapter
# (sitl/mavlink_adapter_node.py) uploads each policy generation's keep-out
# zones through /mavros/geofence/push as exclusion polygons / circles. They
# are the zones as authored, without the Shield's margin_m; only zones whose
# altitude band covers 0 .. FENCE_ALT_MAX are uploaded, and a zone the aircraft
# is inside or near is held back until it is clear - so the autopilot fence is
# never stricter than the policy, and with a working Shield it never fires.
# With the Shield node gone it does. FENCE_ALT_MAX below the policy's ceiling
# would make the altitude fence stricter than the policy (18 policies in
# policies/ allow more than 25 m), so the Shield node reads the parameters
# back from the autopilot at take-off, raises FENCE_ALT_MAX to the policy's
# ceiling + 5 m when needed, and records both (hil_evidence.autopilot_fence).

FENCE_ENABLE   1     # fence on from boot
FENCE_TYPE     5     # bit 0 max altitude + bit 2 inclusion/exclusion polygons and circles
FENCE_ACTION   1     # Copter: RTL or Land
FENCE_ALT_MAX  30    # m; above the demo ceiling (20 m); raised at take-off if needed
FENCE_MARGIN   2     # m, ArduPilot default
FENCE_RADIUS   300   # m; unused while bit 1 (circle around home) is off

# The fence must act on a BREACH only, not steer. ArduCopter's simple
# avoidance (AVOID_ENABLE bit 0 "UseFence", on by default) also uses the fence
# and, in GUIDED velocity control (ArduCopter/mode_guided.cpp, the
# copter.avoid.adjust_velocity call), bends every velocity setpoint that
# points within FENCE_MARGIN of a zone. With it on, the 2026-10-06 shield-off
# run stopped about 2 m short of the no-fly zone for 20 s - the autopilot
# doing the Shield's job - and a Shield-on run would be measured with a second
# filter behind it. 0 = no avoidance; the Shield is the only filter, the fence
# the backstop.
AVOID_ENABLE   0
